comments.content:
Hand-forward from architect-4ae016fb, 2026-10-29, for whoever plans CQ-I06.

1. New producer row. CQ-I03 was split by SPIDR. CQ-I03a (task-c0b0775f) now delivers scripts/local-runner/vm-control.mjs: `<status|reconcile|cleanup> --project <abs>`, which prints one JSON line with schema moe-vm-status-v1, moe-vm-reconcile-v1 or moe-vm-cleanup-v1. I03 depends on it, and I05 (VS Code) consumes the same contract. I06 reaches it transitively through I03.

2. CI wiring is owed here. .github/workflows/ci.yml's 'Test local runner prerequisite bundles' step lists its test files explicitly. I03a could not add scripts/tests/local-runner-vm-control.test.mjs to it, because CQ-V04b1 and CQ-V04b (both unlanded) hold ci.yml. Add that file to the step in I06, after both have landed.

3. Things to check in the hardening pass:
   - ownedLedgerDir must resolve the same directory for D:/x, D:\x and /mnt/d/x;
   - cleanup deletes only ledger-owned VMs whose owner attempt is not the task's open attempt and whose lease is free;
   - cleanup needs Node 22+ for the global WebSocket. On older Node it preserves everything with DAEMON_UNREACHABLE;
   - the lease race between list_resources and the delete is a documented residual.

executionContract.intendedBehavior:
Close the CQ-I client epic once R13, V12, I06e and I06f are DONE:
- record DoD 3's certified-host half per platform and arch from CQ-R13's landed certification, never inferred;
- give every open client residual an owner, including the latestCheckRun.outcome rendering;
- keep I06f's DoD 1-2 evidence fresh by re-running when client, runner or package inputs moved after I06f;
- pass the fresh DoD 4 gradle gate.
No runtime change beyond a bounded fix-forward. Steps 1-2 and 3A-B/4 of the rev-2 plan were re-sliced to b556875e (landed), CQ-I06e and CQ-I06f.

implementationPlan.description:
ADVERSARIAL WHOLE-EPIC REVIEW, once, last. Load adversarial-self-review. Read the whole CQ-I diff: list the commits for I01, I02, I03a, I03, I04, I05, I06a, I06b and I06c with `git log moe/work-2026-10-24 --grep 'Moe-Task: <id>'`. Hunt for what the slices got wrong about each other.
- Producer/consumer drift:
  - vm-control schemas and codes against both decoders. Codes without specific text render 'unknown code <CODE>'; confirm that this is consistent;
  - approval revision semantics;
  - CLIENT_HELLO: the daemon supports it and no IDE sends it, by decision. Confirm that the F04b token-free refusal stays actionable in both IDEs.
- Activation surface:
  - grep both clients: no path sends executionProfile or deliveryPolicy in UPDATE_SETTINGS;
  - no IDE offers verified-local, and the strong profile is always blocked.
- Reconnect:
  - a disconnect while an approval is pending is not confirmed in either IDE (the corpus rows);
  - the daemon resets per-socket negotiation on reconnect (I01 tests).
- Windows:
  - vm-control receives project paths with spaces and drive letters as argument arrays, with no shell (JetBrains ProcessBuilder list, VS Code execFile array);
  - note the Windows-vs-WSL ledger split.
- Packaging: no test artifacts, and every required helper is present (runs 5 and 10).
- Residuals: give each one an owning task id, or mark it 'unowned: human decision'. Search with moe.search_tasks first. Known so far:
  - profile/evidence status UI (I02 note; depends on V06);
  - the JetBrains transient re-arm after PLAN_REVISION_MISMATCH (no codeName plumbing);
  - VS Code's JSON.parse accepting lossy literals the daemon never emits;
  - cleanup preserving everything below Node 22 and on bindHost 0.0.0.0;
  - the npm moe-proxy package shipping compiled tests;
  - SettingsPanel showing 'Settings saved.' when the send failed (I04 note);
  - five producer codes with no bundle text.
  File new defect tasks only for real defects, outside this epic unless they break DoD 1 or 2; in that case, report_blocked on them.
- Rails: no .moe edits, no Git writes, none of globalRails.forbiddenPatterns in the epic diff, and verified-local untouched.
Then write the Serena memory 'task-task-4e412148225f480c8c0d5a1706a3cc76-handoff' covering the evidence for each run, the owner of each residual, and what remains uncertified.
